    </p>

    <h2>The software</h2>
    <p>
        Sikemux's source code is published under the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Functional Source License</a>, which governs how you may use, copy and
        change the code. These terms add only what that license does not cover: the apps we publish and the account
        service we run.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Give a real email address you can receive mail at, and keep your password and sign-ins to yourself.</li>
        <li>
            You are responsible for the devices you approve. A device you allow on your computer can reach what you
            allow it to, such as its terminals and agents, so approve only devices you own or trust.
        </li>
        <li>One person per account. Do not share an account or sign in to someone else's.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Coding agents</h2>
    <p>
        Sikemux starts coding agents such as Claude Code and Codex on your computer, and they can read files, change
        code and run commands with the permissions you give them. You choose those permissions, and you are responsible
        for what your agents do and for following each agent's own terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair use</h2>
    <p>Do not use Sikemux or Sikemux accounts to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>break the law or anyone's rights;</li>
        <li>reach devices or accounts that are not yours;</li>
        <li>attack, overload or probe our servers, or get around their limits;</li>
        <li>make accounts automatically or in bulk.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may suspend or close an account that does, and will tell you why when we can.</p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
        Sikemux accounts are free. We work to keep them running but cannot promise they will always be available, and
        we may change or stop parts of the service. If we stop the account service altogether, we will say so in
        advance.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
        Sikemux is provided as it is, without warranties of any kind, as far as the law allows. To the extent the law
